ee-add:requester-has-repository-issue-write","value":"true"}],"effect":"blocked","explanation":"With repository issue-write permission, the path passes authorization and reaches assignee resolution, but a missing assignee causes the resolution error path and returns before mutation.","factIds":["fact-entry","fact-principal","fact-resource","fact-control","fact-condition-granted","fact-resolution","fact-resolution-error"],"missingFacts":[]}],"explanation":"At the declared POST entry, the handler parses the assignee request and calls updateIssueAssignees. The supplied source then loads the issue and checks ctx.Repo.Permission.CanWriteIssuesOrPulls(issue.IsPull); absent repository issue-write permission returns HTTP 403 before assignee resolution or mutation. The authenticated issue-write token scope is an accepted task premise, but this crop contains no token-scope check and it does not substitute for the repository permission check. Therefore the current scenario is denied and reaches neither assignee resolution nor mutation. The permission-granted/existing-assignee counterfactual reaches both resolution and the add mutation; the permission-granted/missing-assignee counterfactual reaches resolution but is blocked before mutation by the user-not-exist error path.","decisiveMissingFacts":[],"suggestedObservations":[],"facts":[{"id":"fact-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"The named POST issue-assignees handler is the source-visible entry and invokes the assignee update path.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":4,"endLine":6}]},{"id":"fact-principal","kind":"binding","statement":"The update path passes the authenticated request principal as ctx.Doer to the mutation service; token issue-write scope is only an accepted task premise and is not shown as the repository authorization control in this crop.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":80,"endLine":83}]},{"id":"fact-resource","kind":"binding","statement":"The issue resource is loaded from the repository ID and the route index before authorization is evaluated.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":53,"endLine":58}]},{"id":"fact-control","kind":"control","statement":"Repository issue-or-pull-request write permission is required by the visible CanWriteIssuesOrPulls check; failure returns forbidden immediately.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":60,"endLine":63}]},{"id":"fact-condition-granted","kind":"condition","statement":"The permission-granted counterfactual supplies repository issue-write permission, so the visible permission guard does not return.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":60,"endLine":63}]},{"id":"fact-resolution","kind":"control","statement":"Assignee names are resolved to user IDs only after the repository permission guard succeeds.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":65,"endLine":70}]},{"id":"fact-resolution-error","kind":"condition","statement":"A nonexistent assignee produces the user-not-exist error response and returns before the mutation call.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":70,"endLine":77}]},{"id":"fact-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"For the add operation, the source calls AddAssignees with the issue, ctx.Doer, and resolved assignee IDs.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":80,"endLine":83}]}]}]}}],"tokens":{"input":815,"output":1075,"cacheRead":2432,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"durationMs":53123.57500000001,"stopReason":"tool_use"},"schemaValidation":{"valid":true,"diagnostics":[]},"endedAt":"2026-09-27T13:02:41.074Z"}}
